MOS PostgreSQL Reference Schema v0.1

It becomes the canonical physical schema for our PostgreSQL implementation.

It should have a table like:

| Schema    | Table      | Purpose                | PK   | FK        | Lifecycle | Versioned | Provenance |
| --------- | ---------- | ---------------------- | ---- | --------- | --------- | --------- | ---------- |
| identity  | principals | Actors in MOS          | UUID | —         | Yes       | Yes       | Yes        |
| event     | events     | Immutable event log    | UUID | principal | No        | No        | Yes        |
| memory    | entities   | Conceptual objects     | UUID | —         | Yes       | Yes       | Yes        |
| knowledge | facts      | Semantic assertions    | UUID | entity    | Yes       | Yes       | Yes        |
| graph     | edges      | Graph projection       | UUID | entities  | Yes       | Yes       | Yes        |
| planning  | goals      | Desired outcomes       | UUID | principal | Yes       | Yes       | Yes        |
| procedure | skills     | Reusable capabilities  | UUID | agent     | Yes       | Yes       | Yes        |
| execution | tool_calls | Tool execution         | UUID | execution | Yes       | Yes       | Yes        |
| embedding | embeddings | Vector representations | UUID | source    | Yes       | Yes       | Yes        |

Then for every single table, we specify the exact columns.

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

